yond ticket closure.","cohort":["E3","F4","G5","T5e","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'persist a full peer-confirmation record per managed link (Jira linkId, direction, the confirming snapshot revision, confirmed-at time) — not a minimal boolean'","'S1: define + persist the peer-confirmation record ... survives SNAPSHOT compaction; reconciled with managed_refs monotonicity'","The decision rationale is captured inline in the plan but no ADR/AGENTS.md/design-doc artifact is named as the durable home for this new persistence contract."],"finding":"The plan introduces a durable persisted schema (the full peer-confirmation record: linkId, direction, confirming snapshot revision, confirmed-at time) that must survive SNAPSHOT compaction and reconcile with managed_refs monotonicity, but does not state that this durable schema decision is captured in an ADR or standing design doc separate from this ticket. Future maintainers touching managed_refs/compaction will need this provenance contract documented outside the ticket lifecycle.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f950c62f3bd912b18","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Chosen direction / S1","norm_id":"n1f28203ac9f30a58","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the required within-pass ordering of the peer-confirmation phases: backfill (S4) before snapshot confirmation (S2), both sharing one store instance saved once, and confirmation-population completing before the removal-decline read (S3) consults the store.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The plan lists S1-S4 as separate children with no stated within-pass sequencing; the Approach section does not order confirmation-population relative to the removal-decline check.","Backfill-before-snapshot matters: if snapshot confirmation ran before backfill they would use separate store instances / a grandfather write could clobber a real confirmation (the reconcile.py rationale: 'Backfill runs FIRST for that reason, and saving happens ONCE at the end').","Confirmation-population-before-decline matters: if S3's decline read runs before S2 populates the current pass's snapshot confirmations, a link the peer still carries (freshly confirmed this pass) could be declined or, symmetrically, a decision made on stale evidence.","ABSENCE: the load-bearing ordering is knowable only from the implementation (reconcile.py:546-556, apply flow), not from the plan text."],"finding":"The plan does not specify the within-pass execution ordering among the confirmation-population steps (S4 backfill, S2 snapshot confirmation) and the removal-decline read (S3), yet that ordering is load-bearing for correctness.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f47d93abe0fd39f9a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Decomposition (children S1-S4) / Approach","norm_id":"n6f73565199d4e259","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":["First post-upgrade pass where backfill and a snapshot confirmation both apply to the same link — order decides whether the vendor linkId/provenance is retained or clobbered.","A pass in which a link is first observed in the fetched snapshot AND an inbound removal record for a different-but-related link is being applied — order decides whether the decline reads freshly-populated evidence."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In the Approach or Decomposition, state the pass sequence explicitly: open one store instance per pass; run backfill first, then snapshot confirmation (so a real confirmation upgrades a grandfathered entry in memory), save once at end; and require that confirmation population precedes the _inbound_unlink_one decline read within the same pass so the decline sees current-pass evidence.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In S4, state the backfill's re-run guard and idempotency: it runs only when the store file was ABSENT (not merely empty), reads-before-writing, and skips any key that already holds a push/snapshot record so a partial or repeated run never double-applies or downgrades real confirmations.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan S4: 'backfill migration marking existing managed links confirmed-at-upgrade.'","Chosen direction: 'Backfill grandfathers existing managed links as confirmed-at-upgrade (marked as such) so the first post-upgrade run does not decline every legitimate removal.'","ABSENCE: the plan states 'first post-upgrade run' but never states the re-run guard (e.g. run only when the store file was absent, not merely empty) nor that re-running skips already-present keys so a real push/snapshot confirmation is never downgraded to an assumption."],"finding":"The S4 grandfather backfill is described as a one-shot 'confirmed-at-upgrade' step but the plan text does not assert its idempotency/resumability if the migrating pass is interrupted before the sidecar is persisted (what re-run trigger keys the backfill, and how a second run avoids double-applying or clobbering real confirmations).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f86e3acfe43925a78","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Decomposition S4 / Chosen direction ('Backfill grandfathers existing managed links as confirmed-at-upgrade')","norm_id":"n85d1562b70368fd2","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":["A sync pass crashes after backfill computes records but before the sidecar is written; the next pass must re-run the backfill without producing duplicate/incorrect state.","An operator deliberately empties the store; the backfill must NOT silently repopulate it as if pre-upgrade."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insuffici